name issue_813_audio_padding_as_libwebrtc
describe audio_only_lossy's padding on the audio SSRC as libwebrtc M157 sends it (issue #813): the pacer starts padding at the next packet, not at the GoogCC update, and takes its rates as whole bytes per 40 ms window
duration 30s
video off
at 0s capacity=500kbps delay=40ms jitter=10ms loss=10%
# libwebrtc M157 on audio_only_lossy seed 1 (parity-data traces): 851 padding packets, 49.1 kbps, sizes p50 238 B,
# max 303 B. main before #813: 1795 packets, 121.8 kbps. With #813 the forward-link trace is libwebrtc's packet for
# packet (2357 packets: send time, size, kind and outcome). The 10-seed spread is wide on both stacks (ours 5-141 kbps).
expect net.padding_media_ssrc_packets <= 900
expect net.padding_media_ssrc_packets >= 800
expect net.padding_kbps < 60
expect net.padding_size_max_b <= 303
expect audio.interruptions == 0
